---
/**
 * The docs shell's theme rule (Story 53.1, spec-pyforge-herald CAP-63; operator ruling 2026-11-22): the stored theme,
 * else dark -- the rule every other page takes from `themeScript(true)` in `src/lib/site-header.ts`. Registered in
 * astro.config.mjs in place of Starlight's ThemeProvider while `pyforge.herald.site_shell` is on. The header's toggle
 * (`pf-shell.js`) writes the stored theme; Starlight's theme select is not rendered, so `updatePickers` has no work.
 */
---

<script is:inline>
  window.StarlightThemeProvider = (() => {
    let stored = null;
    try {
      stored = localStorage.getItem('starlight-theme');
    } catch (e) {
      stored = null;
    }
    document.documentElement.dataset.theme = stored === 'light' ? 'light' : 'dark';
    return { updatePickers() {} };
  })();
</script>
